# Git LFS tracking
#
# Only the large raw chemoproteomics workbooks live in LFS. They are rebuild
# inputs (never read at runtime) and are kept in the repo so the reformatted
# Backus source cannot be lost again.
#
# After clone, materialise them with:
#   git lfs install
#   git lfs pull
data/raw/*.xlsx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Release archives
#
# Zenodo archives GitHub's zipball, and zipballs do not resolve LFS pointers:
# the two workbooks above would appear in a released archive as ~130-byte text
# stubs rather than files. A missing file that the documentation explains is
# honest; a stub that looks like a 118 MB spreadsheet is a trap for whoever
# downloads it. They are excluded from archives instead.
#
# Nothing at runtime is affected. data/raw/ is already outside the deployment
# bundle (see docs/scripts/deploy_shinyapps.R) and the application never reads
# these workbooks — they are rebuild inputs for docs/scripts/. Their provenance
# is in docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md.
data/raw/*.xlsx export-ignore
